// local-flow-review.bml — the review that guides each session toward local end-to-end success.
//
// Reads what the body already writes, where the turns ran: learn/native-turn-queue.jsonl (the local work
// offered); the native-turn ledger of this checkout and of the walk checkout the day-turn schedule names;
// receipts/session-rent-ledger.jsonl (each rented session beside its local tokens); receipts/remote-guide-ledger.jsonl
// and receipts/remote-review.jsonl. Prints, per session and per open gap:
//   local tokens         generated, injected and local review IDs: welcome, grown, never a target
//   local success        local_verified over gaps attempted; band full and the free review read quality
//   remote guide         prompts, only where fcgp-earned? held, with their tokens
//   remote work tokens   zero by construction and by check; null when unknown, never 0
//   remote review        free, in its own column
// and the live phase costs of the latest lane option this host holds. Appends one row to
// receipts/local-flow-review.jsonl, so the next review reads against this one.
//
// The review names one next local repair, the first of these the rows show:
//   contract  an open gap whose checks no candidate can pass: heal the contract, not the lane
//   guide     an open gap that earned the one light remote guide (fcgp-earned?): one packet, one question
//   split     an open gap whose last three options moved its band nowhere: the lane needs it smaller
//   lane      options that ended with no lane result (a nonzero lane exit): the lane's own health first
//   queue     no open gap: the next band-first gap, written from the work the last rented session did
//   turn      otherwise: the queue holds work the lane can do; keep it turning
// The thresholds are instruments, not goals. No provider and no network: the review is the body's own
// reading of its local work (form-stdlib/bml/local-flow-reading.bml).
// stdin: nothing.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
import form-stdlib/bml/local-flow-reading.bml;
section [form.bml] {
 lfr-run();
}
